      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Utah homeowners can finance a roof replacement through contractor-partnered payment plans (often featuring 0% APR promotional periods for 12 to 18 months or $0-down options), home equity loans, HELOCs, or personal home improvement loans. Many regional contractors\u2014such as Roofing Utah\n\n\n\u2014facilitate quick on-site or digital approvals through third-party lenders.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Roofing Utah",
            "link": "https://roofingutah.com/financing/"
          }
        ],
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "contractor-partnered payment plans (often featuring 0% APR promotional periods for 12 to 18 months or $0-down options), home equity loans, HELOCs, or personal home improvement loans"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Financing Choices"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contractor-Partnered Loans: Fast application process during your estimate, $0-down plans, and promotional periods (like 0% interest if paid within 12\u201318 months). Standard APRs typically range from roughly 4.99% to 19.99% depending on credit.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "HELOC or Home Equity Loans: Uses your home equity as collateral, usually providing lower interest rates for larger loan amounts."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Unsecured Personal Loans: Good if you do not want to use your home as collateral, though interest rates vary based on your credit score."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "USDA Section 504 Grants/Loans: Government assistance available specifically for very-low-income or elderly rural/suburban homeowners needing urgent health and safety home repairs.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insurance Claims: If your roof suffered recent storm or hail damage, file an insurance claim to potentially cover costs minus your deductible rather than taking out a traditional loan."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to narrow this down, please share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Are you looking for 0% promotional contractor financing\nor a home equity loan?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you suspect storm/hail damage that might involve insurance?"
          }
        ]
      }
